      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The influence of emotional-pain stress on the properties of the sarcoplasmic reticulum Ca2+-transporting system of the rat heart muscle was studied. The decrease of the Ca2+-dependent component of the Ca2+, Mg2+-ATPase activity, Ca2+-binding capacity and the rate of Ca2+-transport was found in the animals after stress. These alterations in the Ca2+-transporting system were caused by lipid peroxidation and could be prevented by the antioxidant ionol."},
